# ReDD Block — local dev settings (debug builds only).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust as needed.
# Values are loaded by the Rust binary at startup via `dotenvy`.
# Release builds ignore `.env` entirely — these knobs only affect
# `npm run dev` / `cargo run`.

# Comma-separated chromium extension IDs to accept *in addition to*
# the published Web-Store ID (`hhblkhfdjijdinijakbmcpkmdfhoadcd`).
#
# Two consumers honour this var:
#   1. The compliance scanner (src-tauri/src/profile_scan.rs) — so the
#      "ReDD Focus isn't fully enabled in <browser>" banner clears for
#      your unpacked dev install.
#   2. The native-messaging host installer
#      (src-tauri/src/native_host_install.rs) — so `connectNative` from
#      your unpacked extension isn't refused with "forbidden".
#
# Get your unpacked extension's ID from `chrome://extensions` (or
# `brave://extensions`) after enabling Developer mode and loading
# `redd-focus-web/Shared (Extension)/Resources/`.
#
# REDD_DEV_EXT_ID=ofhfncmcnmiifdeimompdddcffehekfl
